ce rate for the resulting Schroedinger cat is calculated and shown to be a significant threat to this macroscopic quantum superposition of BEC's. An experimental scenario is outlined where the decoherence rate due to the thermal cloud is dramatically reduced thanks to trap engineering and \"symmetrization\" of the environment which allow for the Schroedinger cat to be an approximate pointer states.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "primary_arxiv_category": ["cond-mat"], "titles": [{"source": "arXiv", "title": "Decoherence in Bose-Einstein Condensates: towards Bigger and Better Schroedinger Cats"}], "facet_author_name": ["981896_Wojciech H. Zurek", "1011081_Jacek Dziarmaga", "1012500_Diego A.R. Dalvit"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:2987686", "updated": "2025-10-01T10:45:41.996693"}, "curated": false, "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["cond-mat", "quant-ph"], "value": "cond-mat/0001301"}]}, "created": "2025-10-01T10:45:41.705192+00:00", "id": "2987686"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.62.013607&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.62.013607&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.62.013607&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.62.013607&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.62.013607&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.62.013607&size=5&page=1&format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysreva.62.013607&size=5&page=1&format=cv"}}